sed": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`refresh_topdeck` now skips TopDeck events whose tournament name looks like Commander, draft, sealed, cube, jumpstart or prerelease. It also deletes any such events already stored. The two checks the spec lists both pass: `uv run pytest -q tests/test_metagame_topdeck.py` (5 passed) and `uv run ruff check .` (clean). I did not run the rest of the test suite, the web checks, or the ingest/project/report verification from CLAUDE.md.\n\nThe implementer subagent did the work. I read its diff against the spec and re-ran both checks myself. The change is only in `src/sensei_top/metagame/topdeck.py`, and the test file is untouched.\n\n- **Skip on fetch:** a non-constructed name is logged as a warning and counted in `skipped`.\n- **Purge on every refresh:** `_purge_not_constructed` runs right after `store_events`. For each matching stored event it first clears `duplicate_of` on other events pointing at it, then deletes the event's rows from the child tables and from `meta_event`. This is one transaction with rollback and re-raise on error. It logs a single warning with the count, and does nothing when none match.", "ttft_ms": 1796, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 5810, "uuid": "5b7b82a2-919f-4269-9e41-e8e767c99c24", "ttft_stream_ms": 1029, "time_to_request_ms": 16, "first_content_frame_ms": 1029, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
